  "directive_events": [
    {
      "at": "2026-08-23T08:40:12.291952Z",
      "owner_directive": "Implement #2097 and open a PR.",
      "reason": "plan"
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-08-25T06:04:28.641426Z",
      "owner_directive": "Also fold a small UX fix into this PR: macOS File-About shows a version that is not the current one, and the Windows File menu has only Exit with no About at all. Keep the user-facing template in English.",
      "reason": "Two additions. (1) The reinstall notice page is now a repository template plus an ota_publish --reinstall-notice flag, because the decision recorded in spec 8.1 was otherwise only prose: the 0.3.4 migration would have meant hand-rebuilding the page and the tarball from a description. The notice is injected into the ARCHIVE, never into the staged tree, so a checkout cannot be left quietly shipping it as the real SPA. (2) Owner-directed About-dialog work: main.js has no menu code at all today, so Electron's default menu applies, which is exactly why macOS shows app.getVersion (the installer baseline, not the effective post-patch build) and Windows gets no About item. This belongs in #2097 because a version that can differ from the installed one is precisely what shell OTA introduces."
    }
  ],
