      "pattern": "docs/ai-developer/e2e/2026-08-23-shell-ota-hot-update-lifecycle.md",
      "reason": "Owner asked for the hot-update test plan to be recorded as a repeatable e2e scenario rather than re-derived from chat each release. The file lives under docs/ai-developer/e2e/, a governance surface, so it lands under the governance_touch already declared on this ledger. It is scenario data for the scistudio-e2e-test skill, not policy: it adds no rule and changes no persona guide, specific rule, dispatch template or skill. Scope is #2097 because the scenario exercises exactly what this PR builds -- the shell payload, the loader fallback, and the sticky quarantine."
    },
    {
      "action": "add-include",
      "at": "2026-08-25T05:16:48.374811Z",
      "pattern": "desktop/resources/.gitignore",
      "reason": "Two records. (1) governance_touch back to false: PR #2128 has merged, so this branch rebased onto origin/main no longer inherits its workflow edits. The diff against main is now desktop/, scripts/ota_publish.py, tests/ and docs/ only, with no .github/workflows file, so the declaration would over-claim review scope this change does not need. (2) desktop/resources/ota-config.json was committed by accident while building a local test client; it is generated by the staging scripts at build time and a committed copy carries whatever channel the last local build used. Untracked and added to desktop/resources/.gitignore so it cannot recur."
    },
    {
      "action": "add-include",
      "at": "2026-08-25T06:04:28.641442Z",
      "pattern": "scripts/templates/reinstall-notice.html",
      "reason": "Two additions. (1) The reinstall notice page is now a repository template plus an ota_publish --reinstall-notice flag, because the decision recorded in spec 8.1 was otherwise only prose: the 0.3.4 migration would have meant hand-rebuilding the page and the tarball from a description. The notice is injected into the ARCHIVE, never into the staged tree, so a checkout cannot be left quietly shipping it as the real SPA. (2) Owner-directed About-dialog work: main.js has no menu code at all today, so Electron's default menu applies, which is exactly why macOS shows app.getVersion (the installer baseline, not the effective post-patch build) and Windows gets no About item. This belongs in #2097 because a version that can differ from the installed one is precisely what shell OTA introduces."
    },
    {
      "action": "add-include",
      "at": "2026-08-25T06:24:26.012631Z",
      "pattern": "desktop/resources/.gitignore",
      "reason": "Restoring an accidental deletion and declaring one intentional edit under desktop/resources/. (1) desktop/resources/python/.gitkeep is tracked on main and was deleted when I wiped desktop/resources/python to rebuild the bundled interpreter during the 2026-08-25 test session; a subsequent git add -A swept the deletion into a commit. It is the placeholder that keeps the directory in the tree against the python/* ignore rule, so it is restored rather than declared. (2) desktop/resources/.gitignore gains an ota-config.json rule: that file is written by the staging scripts at build time and a copy committed from a local test build carries that build's channel, which is how it briefly ended up tracked here."
    }
